==German==

===Etymology===
From {{der|de|nds|Kote}}, from {{der|de|gml|kote}}, from {{der|de|gem-pro|*kutan}}, {{m|gem-pro|*kuta-||shed}}, whence also {{cog|nl|kot}}, {{cog|en|cot}}, {{m|en|cottage}}. The ''a-''spelling reflects the merger of ''ā'' and ''ō'' in some dialects of modern Low German; it was possibly standardised in order to avoid the similarity with {{m|de|Kot|t=excrement}}.

The word may be of non-Indo-European origin and is perhaps derived from {{der|de|urj-pro|*kota}}; compare {{der|de|fi|kota||hut, house}} and {{der|de|hu|ház||house}}. On the other hand, compare {{cog|goh|hutta}}, whence {{m+|de|Hütte}}, {{m+|nl|hut}}, {{m+|en|hut}}.<ref>{{R:gem:EDPG|kuta|313-14}}</ref>

